@@ -200,6 +200,14 @@ names, types, and descriptions. The summary below is for orientation only.
 
 ## Development
 
+### Trusted local tool providers
+
+This integration branch adds provider API version 1 to the existing server. A local plugin may call registerToolProvider with apiVersion, id, namespaced tool definitions and an async execute handler. The method returns a disposal function. The provider ID must already be in the host's locally configured enabledToolProviders list; remote MCP calls cannot enable or register providers. Duplicate IDs and tools outside the provider's normalized prefix are rejected. Class-instance handlers retain their binding.
+
+Definitions and dispatch use the same registry and recheck local enablement. Existing HTTP authentication and built-in note tools/ACLs remain in place. Providers enforce their own additional operation policies; registration is trust in local code, not an OS sandbox. The Source Scraper provider produces findings and read-only drafts and cannot write vault notes. Only the separate note connector may perform the user's explicitly requested note changes.
+
+Restart/reconnect a client with a cached tool inventory after installing or changing providers. Server discovery does not establish that an already open client has refreshed. This is a local integration build, not a claim of an upstream released provider API.
+
 See [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) for development setup, build commands, and architecture details. AI assistants should also review [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md) for working guidelines.
 
